    <desc>Send what you type to all panes of a tab or all terminals of a window.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Type into several terminals at once</title>

<p>To run the same commands in several terminals, for example on several
  servers, you can send what you type in one terminal to others too.</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window, or right-click a terminal, and select <gui style="menuitem">Broadcast Input</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>Select <gui style="menuitem">To All Panes in This Tab</gui> or <gui style="menuitem">To All Terminals in This Window</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>A banner shows how many terminals get the input, and these are framed. To
  leave a terminal out, select <gui style="menuitem">Include This Terminal</gui>
  in its menu so that it is not checked. Select
  <gui style="menuitem">Off</gui> to stop.</p>

